        "title": "Surface Preparation: Flattening, Planing, Scraping, Sanding",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Surface preparation is the bridge between raw stock and finishing. The goal is a surface that is flat, smooth, and scratch-free — in that order. Getting the order wrong (sanding before flattening, or finishing before removing machine marks) produces work that looks poor under any finish. Every finish amplifies surface defects."
    }
